Method 1: Using the Registry Editor (Works on all Windows versions)Press the Windows Key + R on your keyboard, type regedit, and press Enter to open the Registry Editor.In the top address bar, paste the following path and press Enter:HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows DefenderLook for a file named DisableAntiSpyware on the right side.If it's there: Double-click it.If it's not there: Right-click an empty space on the right side, select New > DWORD (32-bit) Value, and name it genau DisableAntiSpyware.Double-click DisableAntiSpyware, change the Value data from 0 to 1, and click OK.Restart your laptop.
