Method 2: Using Group Policy (Windows Pro / Enterprise only)Press the Windows Key + R, type gpedit.msc, and press Enter.Go to: Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > Microsoft Defender Antivirus.On the right side, find and double-click Turn off Microsoft Defender Antivirus.Select Enabled (this enables the policy that turns the antivirus off).Click Apply, then OK, and restart your laptop.
