1.Open Task Scheduler:Search bar.Press the Windows key, type Task Scheduler, and press Enter to open the app.Verification: The Task Scheduler window should appear on your screen.
2.Create a Basic Task:Action menu.In the right-hand panel, click Create Basic Task...Verification: A "Create Basic Task Wizard" window should pop up.
3.Name Your Task:Wizard prompt.Type a name for your task (and optionally a description), then click Next.Verification: You will move to the Trigger screen.
4.Choose the Trigger:When the task starts.Select When I log on (instead of "When the computer starts"), then click Next.Verification: You will move to the Action screen.
5.Select the Action:What do you want the task to do.

Choose Start a program, click Next, browse to find your program or script, click Next again, and then click Finish.Verification: Your new task will show up in the Task Scheduler Library list without asking for any password.
